 rural backgrounds: how strong is the evidence? A systematic review</article-title><source>Aust J Rural Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>284</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14678410</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1440-1584.2003.00534.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wade</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Brokaw</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Zollinger</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Springer</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Deal</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Holloway</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of hometown on family physicians' choice to practice in rural setting</article-title><source>Fam Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>254</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17401768</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rabinowitz</surname><given-names>HK</given-names></name><name><surname>Diamond</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Markham</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Paynter</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Critical factors for designing programs to increase the supply and retention of rural primary care physicians</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2001</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>1041</fpage><lpage>1048</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11559288</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.286.9.1